  "sections": [
    {
      "body": "The metaphysics scope is organized around explanatory dependence and the stability of metaphysical commitment. One strand asks whether full grounding brings metaphysical necessitation, whether truthmaking is a grounding species, and whether generalized identity can explain the relation between essence and grounding. A second strand tests the contingency of self-related and worldview-forming commitments through memory pathology and psychedelic-associated belief change. The resulting frame treats metaphysical structure and cognitive access as connected but not identical: the sources repeatedly distinguish objective dependence claims from the psychological or epistemic conditions under which those claims become salient.",
