    {
      "body": "The evidence base is methodologically mixed. The grounding and essence sources proceed by conceptual analysis, formal definitions, and constructed cases: cognitive-significance constraints, generalized-identity operators, subsumption, and truthmaking counterexamples do most of the work. The personal-identity source relies on a neurological case in which autobiographical recall remains while felt ownership is impaired, using that dissociation to test memory-based accounts of identity. The psychedelic-belief source combines prospective survey evidence, mediation analysis, baseline lifetime-use correlations, and a randomized depression-trial comparison; its own claims preserve caution about selection and contextual confounds. Across the scope, the strongest synthesis comes from keeping these methods distinct rather than treating formal metaphysical arguments and empirical associations as the same evidential kind.",
