    {
      "body": "Several questions remain open within the local evidence. First, the scope has multiple ways to connect grounding with necessitation, but it leaves unresolved whether non-strict truthmaking cases should revise the whole notion of grounding or only a species within it. Second, generalized identity promises a unifying formal tool, but further work would need to show how it handles all counterexamples that motivate necessity and non-strict-order theses. Third, the empirical records invite but do not complete a bridge from cognitive change to metaphysical truth: psychedelic-associated belief shifts and memory ownership deficits show that commitments can be contingent, yet they do not determine which metaphysical commitments are correct. Finally, the missing subspaces file limits hierarchical interpretation of this overview even though source, claim, relation, and topic context is present.",
